{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dac4f1a917a68a3249ffb03b5191c","seq":1,"event_type":"created","timestamp":"2026-04-20T19:12:38","note":"Item created"}
{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dac4f1a917a68a3249ffb03b5191c","seq":2,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-04-20T19:23:33","note":"backlog → open"}
{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dac4f1a917a68a3249ffb03b5191c","seq":3,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-04-20T19:23:39","note":"open → in_progress. Starting implementation: fork Linux path in create_webview to instantiate gtk::Window as a true toplevel."}
{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dac4f1a917a68a3249ffb03b5191c","seq":4,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-04-20T19:34:17","note":"in_progress → done. Spike completed. Outcome: Option-D-as-framed is NOT viable. Substituting a WM-managed toplevel as WRY's build_as_child surface produced: (1) caret still missing, (2) typing regression (keys don't reach webkit), (3) misplaced controls / white area rendering, (4) no WM z-order handle for the detached toplevel. Root cause: WRY's Linux InnerWebView always creates its own internal gtk::Window as a child-surface regardless of parent; webkit's get_toplevel() walks to THAT inner gtk::Window, not to whatever we passed in. gtk_window_is_active() on webkit's enclosing window stays false even if our outer toplevel is active. The fix requires modifying WRY itself (path 1), bypassing WRY for Linux hosting (path 2), or replacing the webview architecture on Linux entirely (path 3). See comment on discussion 019dabf1 and hint webview/wry-child-surface-owns-gtkwindow."}
